# iris's keys that the palette answers, each pointing at a role from theme/VOCABULARY. This
# file knows iris's vocabulary for the selected row and the palette knows nothing about it.
#
# Only the selected row is here. Everything drawn on the page in theme.toml is an ANSI slot
# written by hand, since a slot is not a role, and those keys follow the terminal's palette,
# which Ghostty paints from this same source. The four keys below are the ones a slot cannot
# carry. sel_bg is the bar, which has to be a tint of the page and no slot is dark on one half
# and light on the other. The other three used to be slots that differed by half only because
# the ink and the page sit in different slots on each half, and naming the role says what
# they always meant. sel_text is the tag label painted over the tag's own fill once the row is
# selected, so it is the page, the same answer herdr's chip label gives.
sel_bg = highlight
text_sel = foreground
desc_sel = subtext
sel_text = background
